    "introduction": "Beazley is a specialist insurer providing cover for complex commercial risks, including cyber incidents, professional liabilities, property losses and marine-related exposures. It works through insurance-market relationships and distribution channels to serve businesses across international markets. Revenue comes from underwriting insurance, with investment income also contributing while funds are held to meet claims. Its value to customers lies in specialist risk assessment and handling events that can be difficult to insure through standard products. Profitability depends on charging appropriate premiums, controlling exposure and estimating future claims. Cyber events, catastrophes and legal developments can affect multiple policyholders, making portfolio management and reinsurance important to the model.",
